==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Yiddish slang originating from the Russian word for "winnings," [[выигрыш]] (vyigrysh).

===Noun===
'''vigorish'''

# A [[charge]] taken on [[bet]]s, as by a [[bookie]] or gambling establishment.
# The [[interest]] on a [[loan]] of money, especially for loans made by a [[usurer]] or [[loan shark]].

====Synonyms====
* (''charge on bets''): [[overround]], [[rake]], house take, house cut, house advantage, [[vig]]
* (''loan interest''): [[vig]], rake off, [[cut]]